Fixtures for the vamos `spectre` personality (docs/VAMOS_SPECTRE_DESIGN.md §11; the tests are
tests/vamos/test_spectre_*.py, the oracles tests/vamos/psfcheck.py and spectre_testlib.py).  This
file names the origin, commit and licence of every third-party file in this tree, as the parent
directory's README does for the x-heep and PTM files; the repository's LICENSE carries the summary.

Layout (§11 "Layout").  A line marked * names a directory or file a later phase adds; it may not
exist yet.
  cadnip/          vamos-authored Spectre decks for the Cadnip engine oracle (§11 T3b): <deck>.scs; its
                   committed CST dump <deck>.cst (the dump of the deck without its title line, as the
                   harness feeds it, made by cst/regen.sh with spectre_dump built on NetlistParse.rs
                   d565fd3; every dump tiles its deck with no Error node); expect.json, the operating
                   point the Cadnip-enabled VACASK computed for every deck on 2026-10-04 (VACASK
                   rawfile column names); and BUILD, the recipe of that VACASK build
  cst/             the CST oracle's inputs (§11 T0 "Statements and the CST oracle")
  cst/corpus/      NetlistParse.rs tests/corpus/spectre/<cat>/*.scs, byte for byte: 106 of its 127 files
                   (the 21 left out are listed below)
  cst/expected/    NetlistParse.rs tests/expected/spectre/<cat>/*.txt, byte for byte: the CST dumps of
                   exactly the files in cst/corpus/
  cst/regen.sh     WSL, cargo: builds spectre_dump on NetlistParse.rs at the pinned commit and dumps the
                   vamos-authored fixtures (cadnip/*.scs with their title line stripped, lang/*.scs whole)
  cst/DIVERGENCES, cst/GAPS   the oracle's divergence and gap lists (phase 1, owner S1), vamos-authored
  engine_facts/    E<nn>/{deck, expect.json}: the engine facts of §13's T1 rows (phase 0, owner S0G;
                   E102-E109 and E114 phase 2, owner H; E115-E129 and E131 phase 2c, owner X-tests),
                   vamos-authored, except that E103, E105 and E106 hold vamos's renders of xdm/ decks
                   (Xyce_Regression, below) and E104, E108 and E109 copy e2e/08's, E63's and E64's
                   Verilog-A files; E125 copies E75's, E104's and E66's, E126 E66's nan.va; E127's tran
                   decks are vamos's renders of e2e/15; E128 and E129 read the CMC trees in place
                   (VAMOS_CMC_EXAMPLES, never copied)
  lang/            vamos-authored Spectre inputs for the CST gaps and the left-out corpus files (phase 1,
                   owner S1): <case>.scs with its CST dump <case>.cst, made by cst/regen.sh
  psf/             PSF ASCII files for psfcheck.py (§11 T0 "psfcheck")
  psf/real/        real Spectre output files from psf-parser and psf_utils; PROVENANCE there lists every
                   file with its Spectre version, kind and date
  psf/bad/         eight malformed PSF files psfcheck.py must reject, vamos-authored (its README lists
                   them; tests/vamos/test_spectre_psfcheck.py regenerates them from its template)
  psf/golden/      the PSF writer's goldens (§11.1 "Outputs"; phase 1, owner S4), written by vamos/output/psf.py
                   from synthetic engine output through vamos.spectre.results.collect and compared byte for
                   byte by tests/vamos/test_spectre_outputs.py (its README names the regeneration command):
                   rc/ (psf-parser's 23.1 run rebuilt), noise/, xf/, status1/, status2/, status3/, legacy/;
                   and psf/golden/engine/{vacask,xyce}: real VACASK and Xyce outputs of small divider decks
                   (the decks beside them) that the results tests read; vamos-authored
  spice/           the SPICE-mode acceptance corpus (§11 T0 "SPICE-mode acceptance")
  spice/corpus/    NetlistParse.rs tests/corpus/*.sp, byte for byte (all 62)
  spice/expected/  NetlistParse.rs tests/expected/*.txt, byte for byte (61: sky130_inverter.sp has no
                   dump upstream)
  xdm/             Xyce_Regression Netlists/XDM/SPECTRE/<CATEGORY>/, byte for byte: the 12 Spectre decks
                   (*.cir.spectre), their hand-written Xyce golds (*.cir), the run scripts (*.cir.sh:
                   they carry XDM's tolerances and the expected xdm message counts) and the auxiliary
                   files D1N3940.scs, ipwlFile and vpwlFile; not copied: CMakeLists.txt, Manifest.txt,
                   exclude and tags (CTest plumbing)
  emit/            the emitter goldens (§11.1 "Emitters"; phase 1, owner S3): <case>_vacask.sim and
                   <case>_xyce.cir, what vacask.render and xyce.render print for the hand-built IR of
                   tests/vamos/test_spectre_emit.py (Cond, model groups, the §7.3 worked example, the
                   nested-subckt lift, the Verilog-A letter device), compared byte for byte; vamos-authored
  e2e/             the end-to-end decks (§11 T2): <nn>_<slug>/deck.scs with its aux files (a library, Verilog-A
                   modules, a second deck), expect.json (the Spectre-level checks of §11), engine_expect.json
                   (the same checks in engine terms: exit status, the engine columns names_for gives, values
                   at points of the raw output) and render/<engine>/ (the rendered decks, goldens of
                   tests/vamos/test_spectre_chain.py); 1-10 phase 1b (owner S6), 11-30 phase 2; vamos-authored
                   (e2e/22's deck holds one NetlistParse.rs card, below).  The CLI-level decks (11-15, 19:
                   cpp, command-line options, exit statuses) carry no engine_expect.json or render goldens
                   (test_spectre_chain takes only directories with an engine_expect.json); 12_ade/psf/ holds
                   an ADE placeholder file (artistLogFile) the run must leave alone; e2e 29 has no directory:
                   tests/vamos/test_spectre_e2e_29.py writes its deck at test time from VAMOS_VACASK_SRC
  cmc/             one record per CMC benchmark deck (§11 T3c; phase 2, owner C): <tree>__<stem>.json, what
                   vamos does with the deck, measured by tests/vamos/test_spectre_cmc.py (VAMOS_REGEN_GOLDEN=1
                   rewrites them); the decks are read in place from VAMOS_CMC_EXAMPLES, never copied;
                   vamos-authored
  plan/ *          plan goldens (a later phase)

Gate environment (§11 "Gates", §12).  The gate's run on WSL sets five variables; without them the
tiers they open are reported skips (T3b is optional and T3c opt-in, so these two stay variables):
  VAMOS_CADNIP_VACASK  a VACASK built with -DCADNIP_PARSERS=ON (the recipe is cadnip/BUILD), with
  SIM_MODULE_PATH      the device directory it loads: T3b, the Cadnip oracle on the cadnip/ decks
                       (tests/vamos/test_spectre_cadnip.py, needs_cadnip)
  VAMOS_CMC=1 with
  VAMOS_CMC_EXAMPLES   the CMC benchmark decks, read in place: T3c (tests/vamos/test_spectre_cmc.py and
                       the engine_facts rows that read those trees, needs_cmc)
  VAMOS_VACASK_SRC     VACASK's source tree: e2e 29 (T2) and VACASK's python/rawfile.py checks
                       (needs_vacask_src, needs_vacask_rawread).  Unset, it defaults to the tree the
                       VACASK in use was configured from (CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY in the CMakeCache.txt of
                       its build) when that tree holds benchmark/ring and devices/psp103v4, so e2e 29
                       runs without it; an empty value turns the default off
The phase-2 gate ran with VAMOS_CADNIP_VACASK naming its Cadnip-enabled VACASK build (cadnip/BUILD)
SIM_MODULE_PATH=/opt/build.VACASK/Release/devices VAMOS_CMC=1
VAMOS_CMC_EXAMPLES=/usr/local/src/xyce/utils/ADMS/examples VAMOS_VACASK_SRC=/usr/local/src/VACASK.
Besides these, the optional psf_utils consumer check runs when VAMOS_PSF_UTILS and
VAMOS_PSF_UTILS_DEPS name a psf_utils checkout and its dependencies (needs_psf_utils).

Third-party files
-----------------
Four projects' files are copied here, each byte for byte from the commit named (the commits are
those of the design's §0 "Sources"), and each keeps its own licence (see the repository's LICENSE).

NetlistParse.rs, https://github.com/NyanCAD/NetlistParse.rs,
commit d565fd3e359893fbc4376bb9c7b5608ef786e6bb ("Merge pull request #5 from
NyanCAD/fix/spice-bridge-scopes", 2026-09-14): its Spectre test corpus and the expected CST dumps the Julia reference parser produced
for it, in cst/corpus/ and cst/expected/, and its SPICE corpus and dumps in spice/corpus/ and
spice/expected/; and one model card of tests/corpus/spectre/model/ternary.scs (vto=(temp >= 27_C) ? 0.90 :
0.75) in e2e/22_temperature/deck.scs, whose comment says so (phase 2, owner E1).  Copyright (c) JuliaHub,
Inc. and other contributors; MIT License (SPDX: MIT), whose
text is LICENSES/MIT.txt at the root of this repository (the project's LICENSE file, byte for byte).
The files carry no licence header of their own.  Not copied, because whether to commit files that quote
or cite a Spectre manual is the user's decision (design §11 "Licences", §14 q.41, §13 E88/E101): the
20 corpus files whose comments cite or quote a manual, and var_reference.scs, which carries the same
verbatim manual line; their dumps are left out with them.  They are, under tests/corpus/spectre/:
  arrays_langswitch/  array_expressions.scs array_mixed_names.scs array_params.scs array_sweep.scs
                      err_array_binary.scs err_array_unterminated.scs simulator_lang_spectre.scs
                      simulator_lang_swap.scs
  control_named/      alter.scs altergroup.scs check.scs checklimit.scs info.scs options.scs
                      paramtest.scs set.scs shell.scs
  funcdecl/           comment_body.scs two_args.scs
  include_global/     include_multiple.scs
  julia_parse_tests/  var_reference.scs
The vamos-authored lang/ fixtures stand in for their constructs (phase 1).  No kept file mentions a
manual (tests/vamos/test_spectre_docs.py checks this and the count).

psf-parser, https://github.com/ToonBettens/psf-parser, commit 05021e6e62cdb9aebf1ee1a98609bb4b3a4f2d16
("Testing with pytest", 2025-06-15): its real Spectre 23.1.0.242.isr1 output files tests/data/ascii/*
(38 files) and tests/data/binary/logFile, in psf/real/psf-parser/ under the same relative paths (the
psfbin and psfxl data files are not copied: vamos writes psfascii).  Its Python package is vendored
as tests/vamos/third_party/psf_parser (LICENSE, README.md, pyproject.toml and src/psf_parser/**/*.py,
byte for byte; the tests and the lock file are not) for the consumer checks of §11 (needs_psf_parser,
Python >= 3.10).  Copyright (c) 2025 Toon Bettens; MIT License (SPDX: MIT), whose text is
tests/vamos/third_party/psf_parser/LICENSE.

psf_utils, https://github.com/KenKundert/psf_utils, commit 67971463a7bfdbfdb362376374b68fef379c6f9e
("bump version to 1.11", 2026-09-08): the native Spectre psfascii samples samples/joop-banaan.dc,
samples/joop-banaan.tran (19.1) and the complete results directory samples/pnoise.raw/ (15.1, eight
files with its logFile), in psf/real/psf_utils/ under the same relative paths.  Copyright Ken Kundert;
GNU General Public License v3 or later (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later, the licence its pyproject.toml declares;
the repository ships no licence file at that commit), the licence of this repository (COPYING).  Its
code is never vendored: the optional psf_utils consumer check reads a checkout named by VAMOS_PSF_UTILS.

Xyce_Regression, https://github.com/Xyce/Xyce_Regression, commit d4685581dcd690f701bc281a82ee76bebe5da91c
("Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/develop'", 2026-04-27): Netlists/XDM/SPECTRE/<CATEGORY>/, the
XDM 2.7.0 Spectre translation tests, in xdm/<CATEGORY>/ (the files listed under xdm/ above).  Copyright
2019 National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC (NTESS); GNU General Public License
version 3 or later (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later), as its README.md "Copyright and license" section states,
the licence of this repository (COPYING).  Ten of the twelve .cir.spectre decks are real ADE netlists
("Generated for: spectre", ic-5.1.41usr5).  Derived from them (phase 2, owner H): the decks of
engine_facts/E103, E105 and E106 are vamos's renders of xdm/MULTIPLICITY/rlc.cir.spectre,
xdm/DIODE_CLIPPER/diodeClipper.cir.spectre (with D1N3940.scs) and
xdm/INDEPENDENT_SOURCES/{i,v}_sources.cir.spectre, under the same licence.

Everything else in this tree is vamos-authored and GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of the repository:
cadnip/*.scs, cadnip/*.cst, cadnip/expect.json, cadnip/BUILD, cst/regen.sh, psf/bad/*, psf/real/PROVENANCE,
engine_facts/** and this README; and, from phase 1: emit/* (the emitter goldens, S3, written by
vamos's own emitters from hand-built IR) and psf/golden/** (the PSF writer's goldens, S4, written by
vamos's own writer; psf/golden/engine/** holds the vamos-authored divider decks and the output the
engines VACASK 0.3.4-91-g64489cf7 and Xyce DEVELOPMENT-202610100047 wrote for them on 2026-10-10, as
psf/golden/README records); and, from phase 2: e2e/11-30 (but e2e/22's one card), cmc/*.json and the
engine_facts rows E102-E109 and E114 (but the derived and copied files named above); and, from phase
2c: the engine_facts rows E115-E129 and E131 (but the copied files named above) and e2e/07's
deck_fine.scs.
